speechtext:
1.	Yes;
(a)	No;
(b)	For the reason that a copy of the original letter to the constituent sent May 6, 1980, was sent to the hon. member.
2.	Yes, the Postmaster General wrote directly to the constituent making the inquiry but not without advising the hon. member.
3.	Yes.
There was no intention of being discourteous to the hon. member for Leeds-Grenville. As the constituent's letter preceeded the hon. member's letter by a few days, the latter was recognized as a follow-up and the response given to the constituent was made available to the hon. member.
